<section class="about-section">
  <div class="about-content">

    <h2>What We Do</h2>
    <p>BikeLabs covers three things: gear reviews, motorcycle reviews, and moto culture. Every piece of content is written to answer a real question a rider might have — not to fill a content calendar.</p>
    <p>We test gear across different riding conditions, compare motorcycles side by side, and cover the routes and culture that make riding worth doing in the first place.</p>

    <h2>Who We Are</h2>
    <p>A small team of riders with an outsized obsession with motorcycles. We ride everything from budget Asian commuters to premium adventure bikes. We source gear globally — including from Asia, where the best value in motorcycle equipment often sits.</p>
    <p>We're based in Southeast Asia, which gives us a different lens on riding than most Western moto media. The bikes are different here. The conditions are different. The prices are different. We write for a global audience but we don't pretend the world looks the same from every saddle.</p>

    <h2>Our Standards</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Honest verdicts.</strong> If something isn't worth buying, we say so.</li>
      <li><strong>Transparency.</strong> When we test a product, we tell you how and under what conditions.</li>
      <li><strong>Long-form over clickbait.</strong> Our reviews aim to be the last thing you need to read before making a decision.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Work With Us</h2>
    <p>We're open to working with brands on honest, rider-focused content. If you have a product you'd like reviewed or want to collaborate on a feature, reach out — we give every product a fair test and an honest write-up.</p>
    <p>Get in touch at <strong>hello@bikelabs.com</strong>.</p>

    <h2>Get In Touch</h2>
    <p>Got a tip, a correction, or a bike you think we should test? Reach us at <strong>hello@bikelabs.com</strong>. We read everything.</p>

  </div>
</section>

